<% content_for :title, "#{t('legal.privacy_title')} · Playverto" %>

<div class="legal-page">
  <h1><%= t("legal.privacy_title") %></h1>
  <p class="legal-page-updated">Last updated: [date]</p>

  <div class="legal-draft-notice"><%= t("legal.draft_notice") %></div>

  <h2>Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    VertoNow ("Verto", "we", "us") is a survey product operated by
    <strong>[legal entity name and registered address — confirm controlling entity]</strong>.
    This policy explains what personal data we collect when you create,
    publish, or respond to a Verto, why we collect it, and the choices and
    rights you have over it.
  </p>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <p>We collect different data depending on whether you're a creator or a respondent:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Creators (account holders):</strong> your name, email address, password, and the surveys ("Vertos") you build.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Respondents:</strong> the answers you give to a Verto, plus a small amount of
      technical data used to run the survey — a session identifier (so your progress
      can be saved and you're not counted twice), your coarse location (country and
      region only — for example "GB, Greater London" — never a precise address or
      GPS coordinate), and, if a question asks for it, a birth month and year
      (never a full date of birth).
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Some Vertos may ask questions that request personal information such as your
    age, gender, or location, or let you answer with free text, audio, or photos.
    We only collect, use, and retain this information in relation to the specific
    Verto you're responding to, and answering is voluntary — a Verto only asks for
    consent to this where the creator has turned on the consent step, and you can
    decline it.
  </p>

  <h2>Why we collect it (legal basis)</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Running the service</strong> (contract) — creator accounts, hosting your surveys, recording responses.</li>
    <li><strong>Consent</strong> — any Verto-specific research consent you agree to before answering.</li>
    <li><strong>Legitimate interests</strong> — keeping the service secure and reliable (e.g. rate-limiting abuse), and small-sample suppression that protects respondent anonymity in results.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Cookies</h2>
  <p>
    We use only the cookies needed to run the site — no analytics, advertising,
    or tracking cookies. See our <%= link_to t("legal.footer_cookie_policy"), cookie_policy_path %> for the full list.
  </p>

  <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
  <p>Personal data is not sold. It may be processed by these sub-processors, only for the purposes below:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Nominatim / OpenStreetMap</strong> — resolves a respondent's typed location to a coarse country/region; we never send or store a precise address or coordinate.</li>
    <li><strong>Google</strong> — sign-in (OAuth) and, for creators who connect it, exporting results to Google Sheets/Drive.</li>
    <li><strong>[Hosting / database / email providers — list infrastructure sub-processors]</strong>.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>[Retention schedule pending — see the production-readiness checklist.]</strong>
    As a placeholder commitment: we aim to retain respondent-identifying data no
    longer than necessary for the Verto's active collection period, and creators
    can permanently delete a Verto and its responses at any time from the dashboard.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>Under data protection law (including the UK/EU GDPR), you have the right to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Access the personal data we hold about you;</li>
    <li>Have inaccurate data corrected;</li>
    <li>Request deletion of your data ("right to be forgotten");</li>
    <li>Object to or restrict certain processing;</li>
    <li>Receive your data in a portable format;</li>
    <li>Withdraw consent at any time (this won't affect processing already carried out).</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    To exercise any of these rights, contact us at
    <strong>[privacy / data-protection contact email]</strong>.
    You also have the right to complain to your local data protection authority.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    Where a Verto is aimed at, or may be answered by, people under 18, we ask only
    for the minimum information needed and present the consent step clearly before
    any question that could identify someone. If we discover we've unintentionally
    collected an image containing an identifiable face where that wasn't intended,
    we will delete it.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>We may update this policy from time to time. Material changes will be reflected by the "last updated" date above.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions about this policy or your data: <strong>[contact email]</strong>.</p>
</div>
